%N A397139 Number of Hotelling protocols in a two-person game where each player has n distinguishable moves (e.g. "announce a price", "announce a location", etc.).
%C A397139 A Hotelling protocol is an order of play (e.g. Alice announces price, then Alice and Bob simultaneously announce location, then Bob announces price).
%H A397139 Steven E. Landsburg, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.17102">Some Integer Sequences Arising from Game Theory</a>, arXiv:2607.17102 [math.CO], 2026. See p. 14.
%F A397139 a(n) = Sum_{i=1..n, j=1..n} i!*j!*Stirling2(n,i)*Stirling2(n,j)*t(i,j), where t(i,j) = [x^i * y^j] (1+x+y+x*y)/(1-2*x*y-x^2*y-x*y^2-x^2*y^2).
%K A397139 nonn,new
